title: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Verify › The check finishes and is saved
route: /authorizations/eligibility/verify
intro: When the last step ticks, the demo either refreshes a patient that is already on the list or adds a new row, then opens the result. New rows get scripted answers so the demo is predictable.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: answers are scripted from the member ID and the plan. A known patient keeps the verdict it already had.
---
start s1 "Last step ticks, banner 'All answers are in. Opening the result.'"
wait w1 "Half a second"
decision q1 "Opened from a case that is a row on the list?"
decision q2 "Sample card: Summit, Residential 3.5, member ID ending 4821?"
store st1 "Existing row updated\n'Checked just now', 're-check due' cleared, date of service as typed"
process p1 "The sample card matches J.M., case R-1042"
process p2 "Answers are not asked again\nThe row keeps its verdict"

group gNew "A new patient"
  process n1 "Row gets the next ID: V-1001, V-1002 ...\nInitials and age only if known from a referral or a case"
  process n2 "Member ID kept as '…1234' (last four)\nScripted answers from the member ID and plan"
  decision n3 "Which scripted answer?"
  process n4 "ID ends 1012\nEligibility 'Lapsed 10/12'"
  process n5 "ID ends 9999\nEligibility 'Not found'"
  process n6 "Evergreen with Detox\nClinic not enrolled"
  process n7 "Beacon with IOP or PHP\nAuthorization 'Not required'"
  process n8 "Harborview with PHP\nBenefits 'Limited'"
  process n9 "Anything else\nActive, covered, authorization 'Required'"
  store st2 "New row added at the top of the Eligibility list"
endgroup

process p3 "List counts, tiles and sidebar badge recompute from the rows"
process p7 "Counts, tiles and badge stay as they were\nOnly the check time and date of service changed"
decision q3 "Is the verdict 'Cleared to bill'?"
process p4 "Badge unchanged"
process p5 "Badge goes up by one"
process p6 "Opens /authorizations/eligibility/V-1001\nor the existing case ID"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Result › What the page shows"

s1 --> w1 --> q1
q1 -->|Yes| st1
q1 -->|No| q2
q2 -->|Yes| p1 --> st1
q2 -->|No| n1 --> n2 --> n3
st1 --> p2 --> p7 --> p6
n3 -->|Lapsed| n4 --> st2
n3 -->|Not found| n5 --> st2
n3 -->|Not enrolled| n6 --> st2
n3 -->|No authorization| n7 --> st2
n3 -->|Limited| n8 --> st2
n3 -->|Otherwise| n9 --> st2
st2 --> p3
p3 --> q3
q3 -->|Yes| p4 --> p6
q3 -->|No| p5 --> p6
p6 --> g1
